WEBVTT

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.200
News!

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.480
Oh my gosh, this is huge news!

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.860
Erin's become the one to take care of the baby!

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:44.920
No way!

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.620
I'm not joking!  It's real!

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.130
Then did she skip some grades up to college level?

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.000
Isn't this the first case in the history of Kazalm?

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.110
Why Erin?

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.200
Wasn't Tomura-senpai in charge of the baby?

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:06.400
I don't know.  I only heard the college students saying it.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.830
Yeah.  Let's ask Erin herself.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:12.870
Erin's over at beast-lords' shed.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:22.510
The rumor of Erin becoming the caretaker of the baby spread across the Kazalm campus.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:30.500
Extinguishing Light

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.800
They should still be under their mother's wing at that age...

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:10.330
It's tough being separated, isn't it?

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.840
Why her?

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.790
Why is she taking over my place?

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:48.890
Senpai!

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:55.630
Is it true that Erin became caretaker of the baby?

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.950
I'm sure Esal-sensei has her reasons.

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:11.090
I'm sorry, but could you return this to the library for me?

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:12.740
Okay.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.470
<i>Beast-Lord Imperatives</i>...

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.420
So you're not skipping up some grades?

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:33.080
No.  I only received permission to take care of Lilan for a month.

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.450
Oh, all right.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.830
Then that's good!

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:42.680
I was worried for a second, thinking I might not be able to take classes with you anymore.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.310
Thank you, Yuuyan.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.560
You don't have to be so afraid.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.270
Relax.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:39.930
How long are you going to be out here?

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:41.750
The day's coming to an end.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:47.780
Hey!

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.910
Yes!  What is it?

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.500
I just told you that you're done taking care of it for the day.

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:55.350
Already?

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:58.520
But I'll stay and work a little more.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:02.530
I should finish with the pile by nightfall.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.400
I have other things to do as well.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:10.780
Why do you change the way things are done as soon as you take the job away from me?

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.490
Are you trying to win some points with Esal-sensei?

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:18.320
No.  I don't have that kind of intention at all.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.670
Do you have some kind of connection with her?

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:31.510
Did you use that to become a caretaker?

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.590
I've done my best to take care of Lilan.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.760
It's an important baby beast-lord to me.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:41.680
If it dies...

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.980
I won't forgive you.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:47.530
Don't forget that.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:13.620
Starting that night, Erin began sleeping at the shed.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:28.830
At first, the baby would be cautious of Erin, feeding on itself, but it started to become calm as it got used to her.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:08:05.330
As she observed Lilan, Erin began to understand how it spent its days, though Lilan would not take anything but water.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.440
Erin skipped her lunch again.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.330
She's dedicated.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.730
How can she stay at a place like that the entire day?

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:20.990
No wonder she's considered beast-lord gung-ho.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:30.490
Esal-sensei said beasts know the scent of food when it's nearby,

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:34.890
but if I were a beast, I wouldn't eat purely based on scent.

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:39.370
<i>Mom, what's this?</i>

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:42.980
<i>It smells like dried straw.</i>

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.340
<i>It tastes good.  Try taking a bite.</i>

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.460
<i>It is good!</i>

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.030
Eat up, Lilan.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.460
It's really good.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:38.240
In hopes that Lilan would eat, Erin observed it day-in and day-out.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:00.830
Tomura-senpai.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:07.240
Why are you so dedicated to beast-lords?

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:11.590
You're not even eating your food, thinking only about Lilan.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:18.440
When I was small, I was suddenly split apart from my mother.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.990
It's still young enough that it should be sleeping beneath its mother's wing,

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:47.870
but it was suddenly taken away and is now alone.

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:09.730
Lilan is the same as I was back then.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:15.540
But I was able to live because there was a person who reached out his hand to me.

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:22.740
The person who raised me was a honey man.

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:36.460
When summer comes, honey men go up into the deep parts of mountains chasing after flowers.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:40.520
There, I picked up a large feather.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:43.100
You don't mean from a wild beast-lord?!

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:43.890
It was.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:51.210
The moment I picked up the feather, my interest in beast-lords grew.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:56.450
And, in a cave within a canyon of that mountain, was a beast-lord's nest.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:03.370
A mother was nurturing her child preciously, one who cried for its mother,

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:08.180
and that was no different from a human family.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:16.360
I don't want Lilan to be sitting in this dark place, but to bask in the sun.

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:20.110
That's enough.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.270
I understand how you feel now.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.480
Light...

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:41.890
Light that comes from below!

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.270
Tear down part of the wall of the shed?

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:57.990
Why?

00:12:58.530 --> 00:13:05.550
Erin says Lilan is afraid of the light that comes through the window because of the angle at which it comes in.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:13.040
She said that it won't be afraid if it's a light that appears by its feet, like it did when it would sit under its mother.

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:18.180
What do you think?

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:23.630
Now that I've heard it, I think she has a point.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:29.070
Very well.  I permit a part of the wall to be taken down.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.790
This is a piece of cake.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.110
It won't come out!

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:38.180
What are you guys doing?

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:50.220
Please, don't be afraid.

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:33.420
The beast-lord's...

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:36.880
Lilan's crying!

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:50.120
What's wrong, Lilan?  What are you crying for?

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:52.040
Here.  Some goat meat.

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:53.900
Eat, Lilan.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.980
H-Hey.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.120
Little girl...

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:17.510
Erin-chan...

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:23.190
Why are you crying?

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:28.220
Lilan tried to communicate something to me!

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.820
But I didn't know how to answer!

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:36.790
It's enough of a surprise to me that Lilan made that noise.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:39.200
That's its voice.

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:43.520
Wild beast-lords always made that noise.

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:46.170
So that's its voice?

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:50.350
Please tell me about Lilan!

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:53.620
You said Lilan is important to you!

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.400
It's important to me, as well.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:58.930
I want it to get better!

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.370
You're doing really well.

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:07.280
There's nothing that I can tell you.

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:28.170
That cry...

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:33.170
The mother was answering with the same noise.

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:39.020
Maybe I can answer Lilan if I make the same noise.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:05.220
My dear child sleeping next to me,

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:12.120
have a sweet dream.

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:22.400
My dear child, with a touching look while asleep,

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:29.450
have a sweet dream.

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:39.680
The mountain is far, and the wind is far, too.

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:48.670
Let there be silence in the forest, and stop your crying.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:52.160
Let me hear you talk.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:56.820
Let me hear you sing.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:18:05.390
My dear child, have a sweet dre-

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.370
That sound!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.630
You can't, Kashugan.

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:28.050
I'm happy that you feel that way, but...

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:30.810
Yuuyan!  Yuuyan!

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:34.590
Yuuyan!  It's me!  Open the window!

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:36.390
Erin?

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:45.610
Sorry I woke you up.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.020
What's going on?

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.430
The harp!

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:52.900
Harp?

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:56.290
Erin!  This is the second floor!

00:18:56.290 --> 00:18:57.920
I'm in a rush!

00:18:58.270 --> 00:18:59.780
Erin!

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:53.570
I thought it was a good idea...

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:16.330
Erin figured out that the sound which echoed through the blanket was similar to the sound it had heard under its mother's stomach.

00:22:16.680 --> 00:22:26.640
And she felt that if she could play the sound more accurately, she'd be able to communicate with Lilan better.

00:24:01.780 --> 00:24:06.250
The Saigamul and Sezans were created because the citizens of the Grand Duke's quarter

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:08.740
and the Queen's quarter look down upon each other.

00:24:09.480 --> 00:24:14.110
While chasing after some Saigamul, I meet those with masks, and in the fight with them

00:24:14.110 --> 00:24:16.510
my arrow wound opens, and drops me to the ground.

00:24:16.910 --> 00:24:21.080
The one who saves me is a girl with green eyes.

00:24:21.960 --> 00:24:25.050
Kemono no Souja Erin.  The Sound of the Harp.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:30.030
The Sound of the Harp
